WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:01.301
New tonight,

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.035
a threatening note

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:03.336
and a white powder substance

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:05.038
sent to the office of Manhattan D.A.

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:06.072
Alvin Bragg.

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:07.440
This after multiple threats,

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.074
including bomb

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:09.642
threats were made against the court.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:10.810
And just a day after Trump

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:13.046
posted this since deleted image

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:13.713
that shows him

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:16.149
appearing to take a bat to Bragg

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:16.916
and warning

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:17.984
that if he is indicted over

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:18.485
the hush money

00:00:18.485 --> 00:00:20.420
payment to Stormy Daniels quote,

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:21.755
potential death and destruction

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:22.756
and such a false charge

00:00:22.756 --> 00:00:25.291
could be catastrophic for our country.

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:27.293
Cara Scannell is OUTFRONT.

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:27.961
Cara.

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:29.529
More than reminiscent, of course,

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:30.864
of what he said and tweeted

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:32.265
before January six.

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:33.133
What else do you know

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:35.201
about the threat today to the D.A.

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:36.369
and his office?

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:37.270
Well, Erin, sources

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.372
tell us that a 911

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:41.174
call came in around noon,

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:42.842
that the DA's office had received

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:44.010
a suspicious package

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.779
containing a white sort of

00:00:45.779 --> 00:00:47.280
white powdery substance

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.616
and a threatening letter to Bragg

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:51.451
We're told that from the DA's office

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:52.318
that this was

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:54.387
then transported to the NYPD

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:55.855
and the city's Department

00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:57.390
of Environmental Protection.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.092
They review the substance and determine

00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:00.460
that it was non-hazardous.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.462
It's now at the EPA's lab.

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:04.731
And NYPD says the investigation to

00:01:04.731 --> 00:01:06.032
this is continuing.

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:06.633
And as you say,

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:08.601
this is part of a real kind of stepped up

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:09.736
rhetoric by Trump,

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:10.904
really beginning last week

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:12.539
when he was calling for protests, saying

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:14.007
he was going to be arrested and charged.

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:14.340
Of course,

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:15.942
he wasn't arrested and charged,

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:17.877
but that didn't change the calculus.

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:18.044
You know,

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:19.946
there have been, as you say, bomb threats

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:20.780
that are non-credible

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:21.815
that were called in.

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:22.816
There are bomb sweeps

00:01:22.816 --> 00:01:24.484
at the courthouses daily

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:25.652
and that there is just

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:26.586
a general increased

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:27.587
sense of security,

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:27.821
you know,

00:01:27.821 --> 00:01:29.322
whether it's for protests or for

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:30.657
perhaps something even like this.

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:31.391
But we've seen

00:01:31.391 --> 00:01:32.559
I've been down on the ground all week.

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:35.061
We saw an increase in NYPD personnel,

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:37.130
increase in court security officers.

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:37.897
You know,

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:40.066
just showing a little bit more vigilance

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:41.434
around the area,

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:41.768
you know,

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:43.136
particularly as Trump

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:44.537
is raising the rhetoric

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:45.371
on all these threats.

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:46.873
And of course, the grand jury meets again

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:47.974
on Monday

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:49.342
where this investigation

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:50.610
into Trump's role in the hush money

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:51.678
will continue Erin.

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:53.580
All right, Kara, thank you very much.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:55.648
Ryan Goodman is with me

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:56.816
tonight along with Karen.

00:01:56.816 --> 00:01:58.485
Agnes, Filo, former chief assistant D.A.

00:01:58.485 --> 00:01:59.519
for then Manhattan D.A.

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:00.019
Cy Vance.

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:00.420
So, of course,

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:01.621
I know you worked on this as well,

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:03.022
criminal defense attorney now.

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:04.924
So you did used to work at this office.

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:06.359
So when you hear this today

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:08.228
in the context of these Twitter threats

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:09.929
and everything else that's happening.

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:11.264
How old are you?

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:14.033
Well, he has committed new crimes.

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:17.203
These are absolutely criminal behavior.

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:19.172
On his part with the posting,

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:19.906
the baseball bat

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:22.175
image to hit to album Greg's head,

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:24.944
calling him an animal and then calling

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:26.246
for death and destruction

00:02:26.246 --> 00:02:28.715
because it's just like January six.

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:30.083
He knows what his words mean.

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:32.418
He wasn't calling for peaceful protests.

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:33.920
This is a call to action

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:35.421
to his supporters.

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:37.757
And he has stepped over the line

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:39.459
and committed multiple,

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:41.161
albeit misdemeanors at this point.

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:43.129
But he has committed multiple crimes.

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:45.131
We'll see if he gets charged with them.

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:47.167
But he has absolutely crossed a line.

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:47.433
All right.

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:50.336
Does that impact the indictment here?

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:51.704
I mean

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:52.038
I mean, I

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:52.705
guess I mean, Brian,

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:53.640
I guess I'm saying is,

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:54.274
you know, you've got

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:55.909
these are human beings involved, right?

00:02:55.909 --> 00:02:57.377
A day as a human being. Right.

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:58.545
And he's going to obviously,

00:02:58.545 --> 00:02:59.479
he's trying to do

00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:00.914
what he thinks he can actually prosecute.

00:03:00.914 --> 00:03:02.782
But when you have someone

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:03.483
making these threats

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:04.450
and things like this happen,

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.920
obviously it gets emotionally charged

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:07.820
I don't think it'll affect

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:09.322
whether or not he decides to indict.

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:09.656
I think in

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:10.156
some sense,

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:11.658
that decision has probably been made

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:13.526
long before these threats began

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:14.627
one way or the other.

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:15.662
And so I think he'd line it up.

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:17.130
But I do agree with Karen that I do now

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.298
think he has to consider.

00:03:18.298 --> 00:03:20.600
Does he add to the indictment

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:21.734
or additional charges?

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:23.469
Because he also would, by that way, send

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:24.337
a signal

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:25.371
that this has to stop

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:27.040
and you're also concerned

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.608
about whether there could be a gag order,

00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:29.175
which would just

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:30.443
be incredibly complicated

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:31.110
because talking about someone

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:32.312
who is running for president,

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:33.780
who's out there every day talking.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:34.314
That's right.

00:03:34.314 --> 00:03:36.082
So a very good close

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:37.517
example is Roger Stone,

00:03:37.517 --> 00:03:39.819
when he was undergoing a trial

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:41.788
and he put the picture in Instagram

00:03:41.788 --> 00:03:44.190
up of the judge and crosshairs.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:45.525
And that had crossed a line

00:03:45.525 --> 00:03:46.426
so that the judge said

00:03:46.426 --> 00:03:48.194
we had a kind of a gag order,

00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:49.028
but now we're going to impose

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:49.862
a full gag order.

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:51.197
You may not use social media

00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:53.233
to talk about this case.

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:55.034
So given what Trump is doing,

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:56.436
if you are currently under indictment,

00:03:56.436 --> 00:03:57.003
I could imagine

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:58.137
this would be the next question.

00:03:58.137 --> 00:03:59.305
The next day at a hearing

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:00.440
before that judge

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:02.242
and this looks and this is the direction

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:02.642
it might go.

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:03.376
But then, as you

00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:03.843
say, it's

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:05.111
such an unusual circumstance

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:06.446
it's not just that First Amendment,

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:07.780
free speech rights are on the other side

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:08.581
of the equation.

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:09.649
It's political speech

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:11.584
by a political candidate

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:13.152
for the highest office in the country

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:14.254
that's heavily

00:04:14.254 --> 00:04:15.188
weighed on the other side

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:15.788
of the equation.

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:16.623
So, you know, here

00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:17.924
we are on a Friday night, a week ago

00:04:17.924 --> 00:04:18.558
on a Friday night,

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:19.826
we thought this could be happening.

00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:21.027
Right, or happened on Monday.

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:21.661
Is it is it

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:23.463
is it still imminent

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:24.731
in terms of an announcement

00:04:24.731 --> 00:04:25.765
if there is an indictment

00:04:25.765 --> 00:04:27.333
or if there is not an indictment,

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:28.668
which I know is unexpected

00:04:28.668 --> 00:04:29.936
but could be the case,

00:04:29.936 --> 00:04:30.903
is that still something

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:32.105
that could happen any day?

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:33.640
I think it's going to happen Monday

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:35.308
or Wednesday. Of next week.

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:36.576
I think law enforcement

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:37.844
is currently having

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:40.013
discussions about security and how

00:04:40.046 --> 00:04:41.581
and when would be the safest

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:42.882
and most convenient

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:44.751
time for him to surrender

00:04:44.751 --> 00:04:46.786
And I think based on that date will be

00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:48.821
then what day do they decide to go in

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:50.490
and ask the grand jury to take a vote?

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:52.692
Because too much time in between.

00:04:52.692 --> 00:04:54.394
You see what Trump is already doing

00:04:54.394 --> 00:04:55.495
he's already

00:04:55.495 --> 00:04:57.163
causing his supporters

00:04:57.163 --> 00:04:59.132
to make death threats.

00:04:59.132 --> 00:04:59.932
He said himself,

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:02.902
making death threats and white powder,

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:03.870
all the things you're seeing,

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:04.671
the bomb scare.

00:05:04.671 --> 00:05:05.838
So law enforcement

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:08.007
is going to want to keep everybody safe.

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:10.510
And so they're going to wait to see

00:05:10.743 --> 00:05:11.778
and try to coordinate

00:05:11.778 --> 00:05:12.445
those two things

00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:14.814
as close to each other as possible.

00:05:14.814 --> 00:05:15.782
And so, Ryan,

00:05:15.782 --> 00:05:17.350
this comes on the heels of a legal blow

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:18.451
today for Trump in another probe,

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:19.952
special counsel,

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:21.321
so that a judge

00:05:21.321 --> 00:05:21.721
there ruled

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:22.188
that a former

00:05:22.188 --> 00:05:22.689
former top

00:05:22.689 --> 00:05:23.890
aides are not protected

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:24.791
by executive privilege

00:05:24.791 --> 00:05:26.392
so that they're going to have to come in

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:26.859
and speak.

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:28.161
That includes Mark Meadows,

00:05:28.161 --> 00:05:29.028
who would have to appear before

00:05:29.028 --> 00:05:29.996
that grand jury. Right.

00:05:29.996 --> 00:05:30.763
In the special counsel

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:32.699
probe in Washington.

00:05:32.699 --> 00:05:33.900
So you know, Mark Meadows,

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:34.534
as we know, is

00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:35.468
central to everything, right?

00:05:35.468 --> 00:05:36.369
He was chief of staff.

00:05:36.369 --> 00:05:36.936
He was on the call

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:38.738
with Brad Raffensperger,

00:05:38.738 --> 00:05:41.040
texted with a lot of GOP officials

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:42.375
on the day of January six.

00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:44.177
And that's just what we know. Right.

00:05:44.177 --> 00:05:44.677
I mean, the whole point

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:45.611
that Mark Meadows is what we

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:47.013
what we don't know.

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:48.214
So how significant

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:49.882
is this ruling on executive privilege?

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:51.150
I think it's hugely significant,

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:52.952
especially because the court of appeals,

00:05:52.952 --> 00:05:55.288
if Trump decides to try to appeal,

00:05:55.288 --> 00:05:56.522
will probably just slap it down.

00:05:56.522 --> 00:05:58.291
We know this has happened already before.

00:05:58.291 --> 00:05:59.859
And as CNN has reported, for example,

00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:01.027
the former White House,

00:06:01.027 --> 00:06:01.861
the White House counsel

00:06:01.861 --> 00:06:03.229
and the deputy White House counsel

00:06:03.229 --> 00:06:04.530
also tried to do executive privilege,

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:05.732
but then they testified.

00:06:05.732 --> 00:06:06.265
Mark Meadows,

00:06:06.265 --> 00:06:07.934
like you say, is central,

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:09.001
one of the former

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:10.803
January six staff committee members,

00:06:10.803 --> 00:06:12.538
so that he was our MVP

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:13.106
Without him,

00:06:13.106 --> 00:06:14.574
we wouldn't have had the playbook.

00:06:14.574 --> 00:06:14.907
And that's

00:06:14.907 --> 00:06:16.476
because he partially cooperated

00:06:16.476 --> 00:06:17.377
with them.

00:06:17.443 --> 00:06:19.412
This is about full cooperation

00:06:19.412 --> 00:06:22.081
under threat with the Justice Department.

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:22.915
And I think he can reveal

00:06:22.915 --> 00:06:23.950
so many things across

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:25.952
the gamut of issues.

00:06:25.952 --> 00:06:27.820
Has his path to stopping it run out?

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:29.155
I mean, this is that he now has to.

00:06:29.155 --> 00:06:31.457
It seems like it seems like it. Yeah.

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:33.526
Smith seems to be able to get

00:06:33.826 --> 00:06:35.094
who he needs into the grand jury

00:06:35.094 --> 00:06:35.895
very quickly.

00:06:35.895 --> 00:06:36.262
All right.

00:06:36.262 --> 00:06:37.029
Well, we shall see,

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:37.930
because this is one of them

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:38.698
waiting and waiting.

00:06:38.698 --> 00:06:39.599
And I think everyone stopped

00:06:39.599 --> 00:06:40.433
